INT. WINE CELLAR BENEATH A CASINO - NIGHT

Brick arches. Oak racks. A security camera in a corner, its red light dead.

TEO crouches at a steel vault door with a thermal lance. FERRIS stands lookout at the stairs. LEV unrolls a canvas bag. NADIA reads a tablet.

A WOMAN IN GREEN, thirties, silk dress, heels in her hand, comes down the stairs. She is not part of the crew. Everyone sees it.

He draws a pistol. She raises her free hand.

WOMAN IN GREEN
Don't. I'm the one who killed the camera.

Nadia shrugs at Teo. He keeps working.

FERRIS
Who sent you?

WOMAN IN GREEN
Nobody. I work upstairs.

NADIA
Upstairs as in--

WOMAN IN GREEN
Cage cashier. Eleven years.

He stops unrolling the bag and studies her.

LEV
Why help us?

WOMAN IN GREEN
Because the owner is walking down these stairs in four minutes.

Ferris's jaw tightens. He lowers the pistol.

NADIA
Name.

WOMAN IN GREEN
Does it matter?

NADIA
It does to me.

She sets her shoes on a barrel.

IMANI
Imani.

Nadia nods once. Teo's lance sputters and dies. He sits back.

TEO
Door's open.

The vault swings out. Inside, stacked bills. Lev starts loading. Ferris backs toward the stairs, listening.

IMANI
You have three minutes.

FERRIS
(quiet)
Faster.

Lev doubles his pace. She drops the tablet and helps. Teo takes the door. Footsteps above. A cough. A chair scrapes.

KESSLER (O.S.)
(from the stairwell, old and wheezing)
Imani? Is that you down there?

She freezes. So does everyone.

IMANI
Yes, Mr. Kessler. Counting the reserve.

KESSLER (O.S.)
At this hour?

IMANI
Audit.

Ferris raises the pistol toward the stairs. She puts a hand on his wrist.

IMANI (CONT'D)
(whispering)
No guns. He's old. He'll have a heart attack and then we all hang.

FERRIS
What do you suggest?

IMANI
I'll talk to him.

She picks up her shoes, straightens her dress, and climbs. Behind her, the crew holds still. He listens as she greets the old man in a voice honey-smooth.

Lev zips the bag. They trade a look. Ferris does not lower the gun.

LEV
(whispering)
She'd better be good.

TEO
She's very good.

Above, a door closes. Muffled laughter, an old man's. Then nothing.

Ferris exhales and waves the others toward the service tunnel. They go, the bag swinging, as footsteps fade overhead.
